<title>USA: Pennsylvania budget deal compromise seen soon.</title>
<headline>Pennsylvania budget deal compromise seen soon.</headline>
<dateline>HARRISBURG 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>A compromise on Pennsylvania's fiscal 1998 budget is getting closer, according to observers at the State House.</p>
<p>Lawmakers on a bipartisan committee are continuing to work on the issue this week, and say the differences between the House and Senate version of the budget bill are small.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, students of 14 state-owned universities plan to lobby in Harrisburg for more money. The state higher education system has requested $416 million in state funding over the next year, a $20 million increase.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
